<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-16"?>
<Task version="1.4" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/windows/2004/02/mit/task">
  <!--
    Turns already-stored price observations into inbox alerts, every hour,
    whether or not the app is open.

    WHY A SCHEDULED TASK: the alerts are the one part of the tool that has
    to PUSH. A comparison that only runs when someone opens a page is a
    report, not an alert. The tracker's inline check writes its own alert
    the moment a reading lands; this pass catches everything else - new
    demand-monitor average-price readings, and any reading written by a
    path that did not come through the check.

    COST: zero Browse calls. Every comparison reads rows the app already
    stored (price_history, demand_snapshots). Run it as often as you like.

    ENCODING: Task Scheduler's XML reader requires genuine UTF-16, and fails
    with "unable to switch the encoding" on a UTF-8 file. Convert before use -
    recipe verified on this machine, PowerShell 5.1, 2026-10-20 (the earlier
    XmlDocument.Save($path, 'UTF-16') form does not bind there: "Cannot find
    an overload for Save and the argument count: 2"):

      $content = Get-Content backend\scripts\schedule_alerts.xml -Raw
      [System.IO.File]::WriteAllText("$env:TEMP\alerts_task.xml", $content, [System.Text.Encoding]::Unicode)
      schtasks /create /tn "eBayHunter Alerts" /xml "$env:TEMP\alerts_task.xml" /f

    The PowerShell cmdlets (Register-ScheduledTask / Import-ScheduledTask) are
    NOT used: this machine has the ScheduledTasks module's manifest but not its
    native DLL, so every cmdlet in that module is missing. schtasks.exe works.

    XML is used rather than `schtasks /create /tr` because the CLI splits the
    /tr value at the first space when the quoting does not survive the shell:
    the repo lives under "C:\Users\Agha Moutsim\", and a CLI registration that
    looks successful can end up running a file called "C:\Users\Agha" and fail
    every run with 0x80070002. XML carries the path as an element, so it cannot
    be split.

    The task runs as the logged-on user with NO stored password. It therefore
    does not run while you are logged out. Change <LogonType> to PasswordOnly
    and Task Scheduler will ask for your Windows password, which it stores
    encrypted - do not commit that variant.
  -->
  <RegistrationInfo>
    <Description>Turns already-stored price observations (tracker checks, demand-monitor runs) into real inbox alerts. Zero Browse calls; idempotent.</Description>
    <URI>\ebay-hunter\alerts</URI>
  </RegistrationInfo>
  <Triggers>
    <CalendarTrigger>
      <StartBoundary>2026-10-20T08:00:00</StartBoundary>
      <Enabled>true</Enabled>
      <ScheduleByDay>
        <DaysInterval>1</DaysInterval>
      </ScheduleByDay>
      <!-- every hour, repeating daily: the pass is free, so latency is the
           only knob that matters -->
      <Repetition>
        <Interval>PT1H</Interval>
        <Duration>P1D</Duration>
        <StopAtDurationEnd>false</StopAtDurationEnd>
      </Repetition>
    </CalendarTrigger>
  </Triggers>
  <Principals>
    <Principal id="Author">
      <UserId>S-1-5-21-4027038600-626433640-3063675340-1002</UserId>
      <LogonType>InteractiveToken</LogonType>
      <RunLevel>LeastPrivilege</RunLevel>
    </Principal>
  </Principals>
  <Settings>
    <!-- never stack two runs if one is still going -->
    <MultipleInstancesPolicy>IgnoreNew</MultipleInstancesPolicy>
    <DisallowStartIfOnBatteries>false</DisallowStartIfOnBatteries>
    <StopIfGoingOnBatteries>false</StopIfGoingOnBatteries>
    <!-- a laptop that was asleep at the scheduled time runs as soon as it
         can: the point of the pass is that nothing waits for a page view -->
    <StartWhenAvailable>true</StartWhenAvailable>
    <Enabled>true</Enabled>
    <Hidden>false</Hidden>
    <IdleSettings>
      <StopOnIdleEnd>false</StopOnIdleEnd>
      <RestartOnIdle>false</RestartOnIdle>
    </IdleSettings>
    <!-- a stuck run must not block the next one forever -->
    <ExecutionTimeLimit>PT30M</ExecutionTimeLimit>
    <Priority>7</Priority>
  </Settings>
  <Actions Context="Author">
    <Exec>
      <Command>C:\Users\Agha Moutsim\Desktop\ebay-hunter\backend\scripts\run_alerts.cmd</Command>
      <WorkingDirectory>C:\Users\Agha Moutsim\Desktop\ebay-hunter\backend</WorkingDirectory>
    </Exec>
  </Actions>
</Task>
